course: dictionary
lesson: 13388
title: Heartily
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Heartily is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It has two main meanings, and the words around it help you choose. «The farmer laughed heartily at the joke.» Here heartily means laughing with lots of energy and enjoyment.
explain: Heartily can also mean completely or very much. «I am heartily sick of rain.» Nobody means the rain makes them ill. They are really, truly fed up with it. Ask yourself: does this sound like joy and energy, or like a strong feeling about something?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «She ate heartily» means she ate with a big appetite and plenty of enjoyment, the sentence still makes sense. The word comes from heart, which is a clue to warmth and feeling.
fact: Heartily is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Heartily» means with a lot of energy, warmth and enjoyment, as in «laughed heartily» or «ate heartily».
fact: «Heartily» can also mean completely or very much, as in «heartily sick of» or «heartily agree».
fact: Badger and Rat eat heartily after their adventures in The Wind in the Willows.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The children laughed heartily at the clown's silly dance.» What does heartily mean here? | Sadly, with tears | Just once, one time | *With great energy and enjoyment | Quietly and shyly
exercise: «Mum said she was heartily sick of the noisy game.» What does heartily mean here? | Gently and slowly | *Completely, very much | Warmly, like a hug | With lots of energy
exercise: «The hungry hikers ate heartily after the long climb.» Find and copy the word that tells how the hikers ate. | climb | *heartily | hungry | hikers
test: «Welcome, welcome! The host greeted us heartily at the door.» What does heartily suggest? | Angrily, as if we were late | *Warmly, with a happy welcome | Slowly, one at a time | Coldly, without a smile
test: Ella says, «I am heartily glad you came.» What does heartily mean here? | Glad in a sad, quiet way | *Very much, truly glad | Glad for a very short time | Glad only when it rains
exam: Jayden says, «Heartily always means sad.» Is he right? | *No, it can mean with energy and enjoyment, or very much | Yes, it always means sad | Yes, but only in stories | No, it is a noun for a kind of heart
